@namespace DotNetNuke.Website.Components
@inherits LayoutComponentBase

@*
    The layout for the handful of pages that are NOT portal pages and therefore must not be
    wrapped in the portal skin.

    ErrorPage.aspx, Install/install.aspx, Install/InstallWizard.aspx and
    Install/UpgradeWizard.aspx each declared their own complete <html> document in WebForms
    precisely because they run when there may be no portal, no database and no skin at all. In
    the Blazor host the document is owned by Components/App.razor, so what those pages need from
    a layout is the OPPOSITE of ApertureLayout (which Routes.razor applies by default): nothing
    but the page body.

    Rendering no chrome is the whole point. A page selecting this layout gets its own stylesheets
    through <HeadContent> and nothing else, which is exactly what its original standalone
    document produced.
*@
@this.Body
